Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: fix CHARGE_FULL* on SM8350-class firmware

SM8350-class firmware does not send BATTMGR_BAT_INFO, so the charge unit
remains unset even though charge-domain values are returned by property reads.
Set the unit explicitly so CHARGE_FULL* can be reported to userspace.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1692,4 +1692,12 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 	} else {
+		/*
+		 * The SM8350-class firmware has no BATTMGR_BAT_INFO request, so
+		 * @unit is never populated from the firmware. It reports charge
+		 * domain values, so set it statically here - otherwise the
+		 * CHARGE_* properties are rejected with -ENODATA.
+		 */
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
 			psy_desc = &sm8550_bat_psy_desc;
 		else
